What is a variable in shell?
	•	A variable is like a box with a name where you can store some information.
	•	You can later open the box using $ to see or use the information.



🔹 How to create a variable

NAME="Aayushi"
AGE=25


👉 No spaces before or after = (very important in shell)


🔹 How to use a variable

echo $NAME
echo "My age is $AGE"

Aayushi
My age is 25

💡 Rule:
	•	When assigning → don’t use $ (just NAME=…)
	•	When using → use $ (echo $NAME)
